  "can_do": [
    "I can add -s, -es or -ies to a verb for he, she and it.",
    "I can make negatives with <i>doesn't</i> and questions with <i>Does…?</i>.",
    "I can talk about someone else's routine, like <i>She trains every morning</i>."
  ],
  "summary": [
    "He/she/it statements need an extra letter on the verb: <i>play → plays, watch → watches, study → studies, have → has</i>.",
    "Negative: <b>doesn't</b> + base verb (no -s) — <i>She doesn't play</i>.",
    "Question: <b>Does</b> + he/she/it + base verb (no -s) — <i>Does he play?</i>",
    "Doesn't and does already carry the -s, so the main verb goes back to its base form.",
    "Short answers: <i>Yes, she does. / No, he doesn't.</i>"
  ]
}
